---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import { collectionInstallCommand, skills } from "../data/skills";
---

<Layout
	title="Railly Skills: Skills for Agentic Software Engineering"
	description="Skills for Agentic Software Engineering. Contract, loop, verify, gate, correct: done means observed."
>
	<main class="page">
		<header class="top reveal" style="--i: 0">
			<a class="brand" href="/">railly<span>/</span>skills</a>
			<a class="quiet" href="https://github.com/Railly/skills" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">GitHub</a>
		</header>

		<section class="hero">
			<h1 class="reveal" style="--i: 1">Skills for Agentic Software Engineering</h1>
			<p class="lede reveal" style="--i: 2">
				Done means observed. Five skills where each step ends on command output, and every mistake that slips through becomes a check that fails on it.
			</p>
			<div class="install reveal" style="--i: 3">
				<code><span aria-hidden="true">$</span> {collectionInstallCommand}</code>
				<button type="button" data-copy={collectionInstallCommand} aria-label="Copy install command">
					<span class="copy-icon" data-state="idle" aria-hidden="true">
						<svg class="i-copy" viewBox="0 0 16 16" width="14" height="14"><rect x="5" y="5" width="8.5" height="8.5" rx="2" /><path d="M3 10.5V4a1.5 1.5 0 0 1 1.5-1.5H11" /></svg>
						<svg class="i-check" viewBox="0 0 16 16" width="14" height="14"><path d="M3.5 8.5l3 3 6-7" /></svg>
					</span>
				</button>
			</div>
		</section>

		<ol class="flow reveal" style="--i: 4" aria-label="The loop">
			{skills.map((skill) => <li>{skill.step}</li>)}
		</ol>

		<section aria-label="Skills">
			<ul class="skills">
				{skills.map((skill, index) => (
					<li class="reveal" style={`--i: ${5 + index}`}>
						<a href={skill.sourceUrl} target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">
							<span class="num">{String(index + 1).padStart(2, "0")}</span>
							<span class="body">
								<span class="name">{skill.name}<span class="tag">{skill.maturity}</span></span>
								<span class="line">{skill.line}</span>
							</span>
							<span class="arrow" aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
						</a>
					</li>
				))}
			</ul>
		</section>

		<section class="note reveal" style="--i: 10">
			<p>
				Prose rules get read and skipped. These skills ship scripts instead: a contract the harness can check, drivers that look at the real screen, a gate that refuses a stale verdict, and an enforcer table that only grows.
			</p>
		</section>

		<footer class="foot reveal" style="--i: 11">
			<span>MIT</span>
			<a class="quiet" href="https://railly.dev" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Railly Hugo</a>
		</footer>
	</main>
</Layout>

<script>
	for (const button of document.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>("[data-copy]")) {
		const icon = button.querySelector<HTMLElement>(".copy-icon");
		let timer = 0;
		button.addEventListener("click", async () => {
			try {
				await navigator.clipboard.writeText(button.dataset.copy ?? "");
				if (icon) icon.dataset.state = "done";
				button.setAttribute("aria-label", "Copied");
				window.clearTimeout(timer);
				timer = window.setTimeout(() => {
					if (icon) icon.dataset.state = "idle";
					button.setAttribute("aria-label", "Copy install command");
				}, 1600);
			} catch {
				button.setAttribute("aria-label", "Copy failed, select the command manually");
			}
		});
	}
</script>
